WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.390
Add a second resistor to a
circuit, one after the other,

2
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.850
and the total resistance goes up.

3
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.010
That makes sense.

4
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.350
More resistors, more resistance.

5
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.770
Now take the same resistor and
connect it a different way,

6
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.570
side by side with the first.

7
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.240
This time the total
resistance goes down.

8
00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:20.730
You've added resistance,
and ended up with less.

9
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.950
How can adding a resistor
make the total smaller?

10
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.070
In this mission, you'll build
series and parallel circuits,

11
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.810
and see how current and potential
difference behave in each one.

12
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:34.150
You'll find the total
resistance of each kind.

13
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.050
Your mission: explain how adding
a resistor can lower the total

14
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.300
resistance.
